473	// Records one lump payment from a client and splits it across their invoices that are still owed.
474	// The client's credit (held deposits, then unused credit notes) can be used up first; the shares may
475	// add up to no more than the payment plus that credit, and whatever of the payment is left over is
476	// kept as credit for the client. With the deposit source it
477	// instead puts part of the client's held deposits toward those invoices, split the same way; the
478	// shares may not add up to more than is held.
